WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.640
[Music]

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:18.360
[Dr. Garcia:] I am Celso-Ramon Garcia, Professor of Obstetrics and Gynecology

00:00:18.869 --> 00:00:20.890
at the University of Pennsylvania.

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:29.130
It is my position that the oral contraceptives
when prescribed, used, and supervised properly

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:36.330
present the function for which they were designed
with acceptable minimal morbidity.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.880
[Dr. Lasagna:] My name is Louis Lasagna, I'm a clinical pharmacologist

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.160
from the Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:48.890
In my opinion the unpleasant side effects
and the very real hazards associated

00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:50.379
with the oral contraceptives

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:58.759
are of sufficient magnitude as to constitute
a real deterrent to their use as a birth control technique.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.300
[Dr. Segal:] I am Sheldon Segal. I'm the Director of the Biomedical Division of the Population Council

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:07.700
at the Rockefeller University in New York.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:13.700
I shall act as moderator of the discussion
of this important and timely topic.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:31.420
[Music]

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:35.840
[Host:] Welcome to the exploration of concepts and controversies in modern medicine,

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.229
one of a series of programs dedicated to examining
the uncertain,

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:45.280
candidly recognizing that much of today's
teaching is necessarily based upon opinion,

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.280
and that the opinions of eminent physicians
in a given field vary widely.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.009
The National Medical Audiovisual Center believes
that openly airing such opposing views

00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:58.079
is a basic responsibility of medical communications.

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:02.740
Dr. Sheldon Segal, Director of Population
Council, Rockefeller University,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:05.940
will act as moderator of this presentation.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.320
[Dr. Segal:] American women are interested
in oral contraceptives.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:16.930
They are using these drugs at the rate of
over 2500 tons a year.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:22.350
It is estimated that perhaps one out of every three American women

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.880
married between the age of 15 and 44,

00:02:26.889 --> 00:02:29.299
has used or is using the oral contraceptive.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.600
It is being prescribed by virtually every
physician in the country.

00:02:35.609 --> 00:02:40.790
On the other hand, we are well aware of the
fact that women using this drug

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:46.150
are not normal with respect to many laboratory parameters

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.579
of medical normalcy or of physiologic function.

00:02:50.579 --> 00:02:56.850
We know, for example, that several of the
circulating hormones

00:02:56.850 --> 00:03:01.910
are not within the normal range in women using
oral contraceptives;

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.979
this refers to example to the circulating
level of glucocorticoids.

00:03:05.979 --> 00:03:09.780
We are aware of the fact there's an evidence

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.489
of altered carbohydrate metabolism for women
using oral contraceptives,

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:17.350
at least a significant percentage of them.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.060
There's also evidence of decreased liver function

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.970
as evidenced by certain laboratory tests.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:31.810
How is it then, that in the face of this rather
perplexing enigma,

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.859
physicians continue to prescribe the drug

00:03:33.859 --> 00:03:38.720
and feel that they are doing so for the well-being
of their patients?

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.600
These are some of the issues we would like
to explore.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.239
We will first have a statement from Dr. Garcia.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:54.820
[Dr. Garcia:] The ease, convenience and utter
effectiveness of the steroid contraceptive

00:03:54.829 --> 00:03:58.669
is universally felt to distinguish it from
other forms of contraception.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:05.790
Never before in the history of the world have
the untoward effects

00:04:05.790 --> 00:04:09.199
of pharmacological agents so consistently

00:04:09.199 --> 00:04:14.519
and so confusingly been presented to a more
sophisticated world.

00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:21.430
But clouding these issues are the fears of
the unknown itself,

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:28.760
criticisms from the persons opposing contraception
in any form,

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:32.350
and the bias of medical attitudes,

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:40.920
the belief that pregnancy is good and not
associated with hazards,

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:46.150
and then, further, moral issues are entertained.

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:53.800
Basically the education of physicians imbues
him with the philosophy,

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:59.380
the need, to preserve life and to avoid harmful
approaches.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:08.090
This, moreover, is extended to mean that errors
of omission

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:12.450
are less serious, less ominous,

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:20.560
than the errors and the acts of comission.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:24.790
Active contraception, because of this philosophy,

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:29.440
cannot be favored openly.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:34.270
The concept of health however, must consider
the composite

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:40.060
of physical, mental, and social well-being,

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:47.300
rather than mere absence of infirmity and
disease.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.300
The oral contraceptive by virtue of its utter
effectiveness,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:55.940
and the convenience which it entertains,

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:58.390
contributes to the health of the individual,

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:04.920
despite the many disadvantages that have been
pointed to.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:10.920
The irresponsible adverse comments about potential
harmful effects

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:15.780
do not contribute to the health of the individual.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:20.410
Many of these accusations have been made.

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:28.090
Moreover, an unabated population press is
also menacing.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:34.160
Actions of the pill affect all body systems
to a greater or lesser degree.

00:06:34.170 --> 00:06:40.000
These actions are a resultant of the combination
of the end results

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:46.910
of both direct effects on target organs as
well as the indirect effects,

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:55.720
which are mediated by alterations induced
in the endocrinologically active areas.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:00.060
The metabolic alterations that have been discussed

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.750
and pointed to as occurring with the use of
the oral contraceptives

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:10.930
have all been shown to be reversible when
these agents are discontinued.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:15.240
Many of the reported effects are very difficult
to classify

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:20.240
as to whether they are drug-induced or nondrug-induced.

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:25.220
Causality and association may not be synonymous.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:32.680
The epidemiologic studies of themselves do
not resolve the matter convincingly,

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:38.010
Although there are massive data, there are
no truly comparative studies

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:41.050
nor are the statistics of sufficient validity

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:47.800
to resolve the association and causality controversy
with absolutism.

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:52.060
Clinical judgment is very much required.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:55.480
Physicians cannot shirk their responsibility.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:03.460
They must use care and continued supervision
in prescribing and in supervising

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:09.020
and caring for the subjects using this form
of contraception.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:20.330
There is no effective, no more effective approach
to contraception that can be pointed to,

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:26.520
and prevention of pregnancy must be considered an all-or-none principle.

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:32.169
The purported risks of oral contraceptives
are of small incidence,

00:08:32.169 --> 00:08:37.019
and by and large are outweighed by the apparent
risks

00:08:37.019 --> 00:08:42.060
associated with pregnancy and even the toll
of daily living.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:47.660
No pharmacological agent can be considered
to be totally safe.

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:59.010
Individuality is cherished, making an ideal
contraceptive almost impossible to achieve.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:02.330
Many more effective and convenient ones are
needed.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:07.100
[Dr. Segal:] Dr. Lasagna, would you make your
opening statement please?

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:12.400
[Dr. Lasagna:] Yes, since the beginning of
the modern era of chemotherapy,

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.200
since the time of Paul Ehrlich, let us say,

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.089
those interested in the development of new
chemicals have been searching for magic bullets,

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:24.610
for drugs that would pick out the offending
microorganism

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:28.100
or would hit a specific organ in the body,

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:32.260
and leave relatively untouched the rest of
the body,

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:35.670
leave the patient relatively unharmed.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:39.150
Almost without exception, perhaps without
exception one should say,

00:09:39.150 --> 00:09:43.370
this dream of a magic bullet has not been
fulfilled.

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:47.430
Drugs are more like buckshot than they are
like magic bullets,

00:09:47.430 --> 00:09:50.640
and the oral contraceptives in my opinion
illustrate this beautifully.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:55.880
As has been already said, they seem to hit
almost every cell in the body.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:10:01.110
With each passing year we have become aware
of the ability

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.290
of these chemicals to affect many parts of
the body.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:09.080
We have heard of changes in the skin, changes
in the hair,

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.520
alterations in libido,

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.120
not always in the appropriate direction.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.640
We've heard of changes in the liver,

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:18.320
disturbances in blood-clotting,

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.000
with thromboembolic phenomena manifesting themselves

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:23.760
in various parts of the body.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:28.940
We've heard of depression apparently associated

00:10:28.940 --> 00:10:30.800
with some women with the use of the pill.

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.850
We've heard of severe and excruciating migrainous
headaches

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:38.660
developing in some women for the first time
on starting oral contraceptives.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:43.550
We are now beginning to develop more and more
a fear

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:49.620
of the potential for development of cancer
in either the breasts or the genital tract

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:55.820
in women exposed for years to these hormones.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:58.920
Now, when one takes all of those reports,

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:04.320
and this buckshot capacity of these powerful
chemicals,

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:10.620
and combines that with the knowledge that
other methods of contraception are available,

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:14.160
which, while are not quite as effective as
the oral contraceptives,

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:19.640
are nevertheless, in the hands of many women, extraordinarily effective,

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:25.839
I believe it irresponsible for a physician
to look upon these pills

00:11:25.839 --> 00:11:32.960
as a method of first choice for most or all
women desiring birth control.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:40.180
[Dr. Segal:] Well, we have an interesting
situation here in which Dr. Lasagna,

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:44.980
you believe that it's irresponsible for physicians
to be prescribing the pill

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.940
as the contraceptive of first choice,

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:51.230
and you Dr. Garcia, believe that it's irresponsible

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.250
to be criticizing the potential hazards of
the pill.

00:11:56.440 --> 00:12:01.500
[Dr. Lasagna:] I said not for all women as
a method of first choice,

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:06.220
I believe it is the method of first choice
for some.

00:12:06.230 --> 00:12:06.240
[Dr. Segal:] Right.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:11.270
I think that there probably exists a difficulty
here

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:19.180
in defining just what the precise position
of each discussant is.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:27.080
Perhaps I could help to resolve this by asking
two pointed questions, one to each of you.

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:31.730
To you, Dr. Lasagna, I would ask do you believe
that the oral contraceptives

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:36.070
as are now being used should be withdrawn
from the market?

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:40.700
And to you, Dr. Garcia, do you believe that
the safety of these drugs

00:12:40.700 --> 00:12:44.930
is adequate to permit their widespread use
without medical prescription?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.460
Dr. Lasagna?

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.720
[Dr. Lasagna:] While I have for some years
now

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:52.500
been beating the drum, trying to alert people
to the possible hazards

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:53.980
of the oral contraceptives.

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:57.920
I have never and do not today espouse to physicians

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:02.000
that these medicaments should be removed from
the market.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:06.740
I think they continue to play a very important
role in birth control.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:18.420
[Dr. Garcia:] There is no question 
that the controversy that exists

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:23.680
is really not as deep as it appears at first glance.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:31.209
On the one hand, it's a matter of how one
weighs out the relative merit.

00:13:31.209 --> 00:13:36.000
There is no question that, as I indicated
in my opening statement,

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.200
that the physician cannot shirk his responsibility.

00:13:40.740 --> 00:13:46.820
He has to supervise his patients adequately,
completely.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.820
He cannot just prescribe the oral contraceptive,

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:57.510
nor can the oral contraceptive be dispensed
over the counter, nor in slot machines.

00:13:57.510 --> 00:14:03.420
There are sufficient warnings from the studies
and epidemiological reviews,

00:14:03.420 --> 00:14:06.850
and while they do not point with absolute
[inaudible],

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:13.170
I quite concur that these must not be left
unheeded.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:18.770
One must continue to review the problem with
this very much in mind.

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:28.080
However, the aspect of the hazards of not
taking the oral contraceptives

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:30.420
and when I say not taking the oral contraceptive,

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:35.850
I am really referring to not taking or not
using really effective methods of family planning.

00:14:35.850 --> 00:14:41.649
And when you get down below six pregnancies
per 100 women a year,

00:14:41.649 --> 00:14:47.959
you are dealing with relatively effective
methods.

00:14:47.959 --> 00:14:54.029
Above this, and most of the methods that have
been evaluated

00:14:54.029 --> 00:15:00.240
and not associated with the need for a physician,

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:05.100
are in the category of being relatively ineffective.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:09.080
And when you're dealing with this, as I indicated
also,

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:18.310
the need for considering the philosophy that contraception is an all-or-none principle.

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.779
When a woman comes to me she, doesn't want to be half-safe,

00:15:21.779 --> 00:15:25.500
she wants to have complete protection, this is what she's asking for.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:30.800
The unwanted pregnancy raises the great scepter

00:15:31.690 --> 00:15:36.180
and I think here we have increases in maternal and fetal mortality,

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:39.140
we have increases in other morbidities,

00:15:39.140 --> 00:15:42.970
we have increased hazards of the induced abortion itself,

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:47.410
even in the best of hands there are hazards
with this approach.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:51.760
There are increases in the undesirable marriages

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:55.529
that might result without the availability
of effective contraception.

00:15:55.529 --> 00:15:58.700
There are also the trauma and other features

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:05.980
with regard to illegitimacy and the increase
in the undesirable parental behavior

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:11.810
towards the offspring, which I've seen with
great frequency in our society today.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:17.810
[Dr. Segal:] Dr. Garcia, I don't think there's
any argument about the relative advantages

00:16:17.810 --> 00:16:23.230
to the woman and to society at large derived
from the use of contraception.

00:16:23.230 --> 00:16:29.300
I think it's sometimes unfortunate that people
consider as synonyms

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:33.029
contraception on the one hand and oral contraception
on the other.

00:16:33.029 --> 00:16:37.399
Many of the benefits in terms of maternal
health of which you speak

00:16:37.399 --> 00:16:42.610
are derived from virtually all effective contraception,

00:16:42.610 --> 00:16:49.680
and for women in many of our socioeconomic
classes, effective contraception includes

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:55.550
not only oral contraception but the intelligent
use of the diaphragm,

00:16:55.550 --> 00:16:57.290
use of the intrauterine device,

00:16:57.290 --> 00:17:01.890
and in fact the intelligent use of the method
of periodic abstinence.

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:06.799
But I think that from the response that both
of you made,

00:17:06.799 --> 00:17:16.459
it's clear that you have each weighed the
equation of relative risk and benefit,

00:17:16.459 --> 00:17:22.439
and come to the conclusion that there is enough
safety in the use of oral contraceptives

00:17:22.439 --> 00:17:29.330
to warrant the continuation of its use in
the country.

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:34.989
So let us focus now on the question of these
hazards and risks,

00:17:34.989 --> 00:17:38.279
so that those in the audience can make their
own judgments

00:17:38.279 --> 00:17:42.249
about this balance of the hazards on the one
hand

00:17:42.249 --> 00:17:44.590
and the effectiveness and usefulness on the
other.

00:17:44.590 --> 00:17:46.909
[Dr. Lasagna:] I'd just like to comment on...

00:17:46.909 --> 00:17:47.779
[Dr. Segal:] Sure.

00:17:47.779 --> 00:17:52.499
[Dr. Lasagna:] Dr. Garcia's statement about
women wanting 100 percent protection,

00:17:52.499 --> 00:17:54.989
I don't think all women want 100 percent protection,

00:17:54.989 --> 00:18:00.600
and I think this is one of the reasons why
there is such a tremendous variability

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:05.690
in the reports in the literature on the effectiveness
of such things as condoms and diaphragms.

00:18:05.690 --> 00:18:12.509
I think the condom and the diaphragm used
compulsively

00:18:12.509 --> 00:18:15.570
represent extraordinarily effective techniques.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:18.440
But if you're casual about their use,

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:22.409
if you want a child or two sometime in the
future

00:18:22.409 --> 00:18:27.919
and don't really care all that much whether
it occurs a year from now or two years from now,

00:18:28.450 --> 00:18:32.139
I think one has a different approach to the
use of these mechanical devices

00:18:32.139 --> 00:18:37.769
than the woman who has had four or five children,
considers her family complete,

00:18:37.769 --> 00:18:42.879
and is darn likely to be compulsive about
the use of these techniques.

00:18:42.879 --> 00:18:46.570
So that I think in the interest of individualizing
our approach to these women,

00:18:46.570 --> 00:18:52.399
I think it would be unfortunate to give the
impression that every woman wants 100 percent protection...

00:18:53.769 --> 00:18:57.159
furthermore, if I can just complete my thought,

00:18:57.159 --> 00:19:01.200
with the oral contraceptives one doesn't have
100 percent protection,

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:05.159
at least not with the sequential ones, which
in my experience,

00:19:05.159 --> 00:19:07.850
the number of anecdotal reports I've come
across,

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:12.720
talking with patients, with obstetricians,
the failure rate is significant there.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:14.629
The protection is far from complete.

00:19:14.629 --> 00:19:20.869
[Dr. Garcia:] Well, I quite agree that one
has to individualize;

00:19:20.869 --> 00:19:27.840
however, I again, the point that one might
take at issue here,

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:31.289
mainly that the patient that has four or five
pregnancies

00:19:31.289 --> 00:19:35.210
could likewise be categorized as being in
the upper age group,

00:19:35.210 --> 00:19:38.720
where she's going to fall within the category
of having greater risk

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:40.070
with taking the oral contraceptives.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:43.769
So it's not so simple a matter, and as a
gynecologist,

00:19:43.769 --> 00:19:47.249
I don't know what your experience is as a
clinical pharmacologist,

00:19:47.249 --> 00:19:48.519
but as a gynecologist,

00:19:48.519 --> 00:19:53.070
when I query my patients they want an all-or-none sort of reassurance

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:57.789
and very few of them elect to take sequential
modalities.

00:19:57.789 --> 00:20:02.960
[Dr. Segal:] Can we pass now to the question
of the hazards themselves,

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:09.210
you pointed to Dr. Lasagna's worldwide reputation
as a clinical pharmacologist,

00:20:09.210 --> 00:20:13.789
so perhaps we should ask him about some of
these issues

00:20:13.789 --> 00:20:18.309
that have been raised with respect to the
safety of the pill.

00:20:18.309 --> 00:20:19.919
Let's take the cancer issue first.

00:20:19.919 --> 00:20:23.919
Where does that stand and what are the real
facts in that situation, Dr. Lasagna?

00:20:23.919 --> 00:20:27.330
[Dr. Lasagna:] I don't think there are a lot
of hard facts to go on here.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:33.039
We have a long background of experimental
evidence suggesting that hormones

00:20:33.039 --> 00:20:36.869
can be utilized in a number of animal models

00:20:36.869 --> 00:20:39.979
to produce things like breast cancer, that's
clear.

00:20:39.979 --> 00:20:43.669
The relevance of these studies to the use
of these hormones

00:20:43.669 --> 00:20:47.970
in the variety of clinical states in which
they have been used

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.840
for a long time is unclear to me.

00:20:50.840 --> 00:20:55.580
I think we're beginning to have reports on
certain changes

00:20:55.580 --> 00:21:03.059
in the cells in the cervix that make one at
least worry more

00:21:03.059 --> 00:21:06.279
than we've been worrying in the past,

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:10.879
and in my opinion, at the moment the issue
is an open one.

00:21:10.879 --> 00:21:16.239
I think with the background that we have on
what these hormones can do in the laboratory,

00:21:16.239 --> 00:21:24.029
it would be foolish to assume that we have
no worries,

00:21:24.029 --> 00:21:29.450
but I also would say that at the moment, the
evidence implicating these oral contraceptives

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:35.200
in the production of any kind of cancer is
lacking.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:38.220
I think the evidence, for example, is much
more compelling

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:40.190
in regard to thromboembolic disease.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:45.619
[Dr. Segal:] Still for a moment on the cancer
issue--on the basis of the animal work,

00:21:45.619 --> 00:21:49.799
isn't it more likely that the real concern is the breast rather the cervix?

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:51.120
[Dr. Lasagna:] I think so, yes.

00:21:52.179 --> 00:21:55.710
[Dr. Segal:] And have there been any clinical
observations,

00:21:55.710 --> 00:21:58.729
or let me put it even more fundamentally,

00:21:58.729 --> 00:22:02.519
has anyone actually done a study that would
give us some idea

00:22:02.519 --> 00:22:05.279
as to whether or not there is a causal relationship?

00:22:05.279 --> 00:22:07.669
[Dr. Lasagnal:] I'm not aware of any.

00:22:07.669 --> 00:22:12.399
It's a great pity, I think, that so little
attention has been paid

00:22:12.399 --> 00:22:16.739
to the setting up of prospective studies to
monitor all these things

00:22:16.739 --> 00:22:22.149
that we're concerned about and that we have
a hard time making definite statements about,

00:22:22.149 --> 00:22:24.820
because we're stuck with retrospective analysis.

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:28.769
[Dr. Segal:] Dr. Garcia, you've been mostly involved with this.

00:22:28.769 --> 00:22:34.909
[Dr. Garcia:] Attempts to set up prospective
studies have been, in later years, tried...

00:22:34.909 --> 00:22:38.509
One of the greatest difficulties, and one
of the things that...

00:22:38.509 --> 00:22:44.940
this is new to most of the scientific world
in clinical lines of investigation,

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:54.809
that is, to sample a denominator that is as
vast as is required

00:22:54.809 --> 00:22:58.749
to measure small changes in the numerator,

00:22:58.749 --> 00:23:01.179
is indeed a task that I don't know if it would
ever be accomplished

00:23:01.179 --> 00:23:02.690
or not with reference to the oral contraceptives.

00:23:02.690 --> 00:23:07.580
There's so many other factors that come into
the bias of selection and the like,

00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:14.940
that it's difficult to do this, and what's
more, to try to have a truly controlled population

00:23:14.960 --> 00:23:21.139
that is not using the steroid contraceptive
versus a [inaudible] contraceptive, is likewise very difficult

00:23:21.139 --> 00:23:24.049
because the steroid contraceptive group feel more compelled

00:23:24.049 --> 00:23:28.269
because of the adverse publicity to come
back to be seen more frequently.

00:23:28.269 --> 00:23:32.149
While those on other techniques are much more
difficult to follow

00:23:32.149 --> 00:23:34.729
and this has been one of the greatest pitfalls that we've had

00:23:34.729 --> 00:23:37.759
in trying to arrange for prospective studies.

00:23:37.759 --> 00:23:38.960
I don't know how to get around that.

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:41.879
[Dr. Segal:] But I think that there are good
epidemiologic methods

00:23:41.879 --> 00:23:44.989
to account for this bias, or to take it into
account

00:23:44.989 --> 00:23:47.919
in setting up the design of the study.

00:23:47.919 --> 00:23:51.849
But let me turn to another issue,

00:23:51.849 --> 00:23:58.269
I think the one that has been most firmly
established among the possible serious consequences

00:23:58.269 --> 00:24:04.470
of the use of oral contraception has been
the epidemiologic studies and indications

00:24:04.470 --> 00:24:10.919
of an increased risk of thromboembolic disease
associated with the use of the drug.

00:24:10.919 --> 00:24:15.619
In studies both in Britain, and now on the
basis of the recent report

00:24:15.619 --> 00:24:20.259
by the Advisory Committee of Obstetrics and Gynecology of the Food and Drug Administration

00:24:20.259 --> 00:24:22.279
confirmed here in the United States.

00:24:22.279 --> 00:24:29.179
Can you tell us how that stands and what your
view of that issue is, Dr. Garcia?

00:24:29.179 --> 00:24:38.929
[Dr. Garcia:] I...there is a strong warning
that this presents.

00:24:38.929 --> 00:24:44.479
I don't know that this conclusively proves
that there is a cause and effect relationship,

00:24:44.479 --> 00:24:50.519
and I think that as I indicated previously,
epidemiologic reviews will not do this.

00:24:50.520 --> 00:24:55.680
They are still lacking many of the mechanisms to explain

00:24:55.680 --> 00:25:02.060
the occurrence of these thromboembolic and other effects,

00:25:02.060 --> 00:25:08.300
and until this gap has been bridged to demonstrate
the mechanism of action

00:25:08.300 --> 00:25:10.380
that will produce the effect,

00:25:10.389 --> 00:25:13.249
we still will not have a cause and effect
relationship,

00:25:13.249 --> 00:25:17.059
but nonetheless these studies are very carefully designed...

00:25:17.059 --> 00:25:23.919
they are performed according to sound epidemiologic
principles,

00:25:23.980 --> 00:25:28.340
and consistently, although with different
variants of incidence and points of comparison,

00:25:28.349 --> 00:25:33.089
we have a concurrence with all of the studies indicating an association

00:25:33.089 --> 00:25:36.189
between the use of oral contraceptives

00:25:36.189 --> 00:25:38.419
and the occurrence of thrombophlebitis,

00:25:38.419 --> 00:25:47.059
and also consistently that risk is seen greater in the older age group than the younger age group.

00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:50.260
[Dr. Lasagna:] May I comment on the quality
of the evidence linking the contraceptives

00:25:50.269 --> 00:25:54.039
to...oral contraceptives to clotting,

00:25:54.039 --> 00:25:57.330
one thing I know something about is the difficulty
of linking drugs

00:25:57.330 --> 00:26:00.420
to side effects that are said to be associated
with them.

00:26:00.420 --> 00:26:08.720
But in my opinion, the evidence on this point
is so good as to be very compelling,

00:26:08.720 --> 00:26:11.960
at least it's so much better than we usually
have for other drugs

00:26:11.960 --> 00:26:14.269
that I think one can't ignore the evidence.

00:26:14.269 --> 00:26:17.419
The evidence exists in my opinion, not only
in the form of epidemiologic data,

00:26:17.419 --> 00:26:19.849
but in the clotting studies that have been
done,

00:26:19.849 --> 00:26:23.070
which in almost all instances have shown a
change in women taking these pills

00:26:23.070 --> 00:26:25.330
in the direction of increased clotting.

00:26:25.330 --> 00:26:28.759
The peculiar distribution of some of these
clots that they're seeing,

00:26:28.759 --> 00:26:33.149
women coming in with clots in the veins of
their arms, a most unusual phenomenon.

00:26:33.149 --> 00:26:35.919
Clots in the vertebral arteries in young women,

00:26:35.919 --> 00:26:39.369
a most unusual neurological picture, and then
the challenge cases,

00:26:39.369 --> 00:26:43.309
the women who develop recurrent thrombophlebitis
each time they're given the pill.

00:26:43.309 --> 00:26:44.279
There aren't a lot of those,

00:26:44.279 --> 00:26:49.389
but there are enough I think to represent
a legitimate challenge type of evidence.

00:26:49.389 --> 00:26:54.749
[Dr. Garcia:] But this sort of bizarre type
of location of thromboembolic phenomenon is not new,

00:26:54.769 --> 00:26:58.580
it's just that it hasn't been focused attention on in association

00:26:58.580 --> 00:27:01.299
with the use of oral contraceptives, number
one,

00:27:01.299 --> 00:27:06.799
and secondly we have to also consider that...uh...

00:27:07.980 --> 00:27:11.499
[Dr. Segal:] I'm afraid, Dr. Garcia, I'm not
going to let you finish your thought because

00:27:11.499 --> 00:27:13.220
our time is up.

00:27:13.220 --> 00:27:17.470
In the few seconds left to us,

00:27:17.470 --> 00:27:22.070
I'd like to attempt a brief summary of this
discussion.

00:27:22.070 --> 00:27:26.070
It seems to me that we have reached a consensus

00:27:26.070 --> 00:27:32.440
that this is a type of medication that does
involve risk.

00:27:32.440 --> 00:27:36.429
Both participants agree that the risk is not
so great

00:27:36.429 --> 00:27:40.909
to warrant removal of these drugs from the
physician's armamentarium.

00:27:40.909 --> 00:27:43.830
I think that both agree also, however,

00:27:43.830 --> 00:27:48.859
that when these drugs are used, they must
be used under very careful supervision

00:27:48.859 --> 00:27:54.909
and although the point wasn't raised I feel
confident that both would agree

00:27:54.909 --> 00:27:58.469
that the labeling instructions required

00:27:58.469 --> 00:28:03.599
by the Food and Drug Administration should
be adhered to very strictly.

00:28:03.599 --> 00:28:10.450
As with all drugs, there is a question of
relative risk versus relative advantage,

00:28:10.450 --> 00:28:12.909
in determining safety.

00:28:12.909 --> 00:28:15.109
On that basis and by that definition,

00:28:15.109 --> 00:28:18.469
it seems that there is an element of safety

00:28:18.469 --> 00:28:25.359
sufficient for continuation of the use of
oral contraceptives.

00:28:28.680 --> 00:28:33.280
[Host:] We thank Dr. Celso-Ramon Garcia, Dr.
Louis Lasagna, and Dr. Sheldon Segal

00:28:33.289 --> 00:28:37.619
for their interesting analysis of a critical
problem in patient care.

00:28:37.619 --> 00:28:41.179
In subsequent programs, we shall continue
to record equally significant

00:28:41.180 --> 00:28:44.720
concepts and controversies in modern medicine,

00:28:44.729 --> 00:28:48.649
The opinions expressed on this program do
not necessarily constitute endorsement

00:28:48.649 --> 00:28:53.989
by the Department of Health, Education and Welfare, the Public Health Service, or its constituents.

00:28:53.989 --> 00:29:27.380
[Music]

